selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#physical-cooling-channel-construction\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Physical cooling-channel construction<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#physical-cooling-channel-construction\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">build_channel_construction(circuit,</span> <span class=\"pre\">reference_path)</span></code> resolves a circuit\u2019s\nnominal winding into the section it physically occupies. The same resolved\ngeometry feeds the simulation, CAD, and the native 3D viewer, so a channel is\nsized once and drawn, meshed and solved from that one answer.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/thrust_chamber/Wall.html#pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.Wall\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.Wall\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Wall</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">material</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">thickness</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">role</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'main'</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Single structural wall or coating layer in a thrust chamber.</p><p>Encapsulates material and thickness information for heat-conduction\ncalculations.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#keep-outs\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Keep-outs<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#keep-outs\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>A surface channel\u2019s angular pitch is by default an even share of the\ncircumference among every occluding channel present at <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">x</span></code>. A\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ChannelKeepOut</span></code> takes part of the circumference out of that share first:</p>", "a[href=\"#rib-projection\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Rib projection<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#rib-projection\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>A simple wedge would produce a rib that thickens toward the roof. The\nconstruction instead intersects the floor and roof circles with the two faces\nof each rib.</p><p>Rib faces run along the local radial direction, so a transverse section shows\nribs that point at the engine axis rather than leaning over. Writing <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">u</span></code> for\nradial and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">v</span></code> for circumferential offsets from a rib\u2019s own centre ray, its two\nfaces are the parallel lines</p>", "a[href=\"#choosing-the-rounded-height-input\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Choosing the rounded height input<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#choosing-the-rounded-height-input\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Rounded sections accept the full internal coolant height by default. To use\nits older base-height parameter, set the option on the cross section:</p>", "a[href=\"#rounded-channels-and-onshape\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Rounded channels and Onshape<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#rounded-channels-and-onshape\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">CrossSectionRounded</span></code> builds its lobes in\nplanes normal to the nominal winding, and both lobes are tangent to the two\nrays that separate a channel from its neighbours. The lobes are therefore sized\nat the radius they end up at: there is no outward translation afterwards, which\nis what used to leave the wrong amount of material between neighbouring tubes.</p><p>Where the lobes sit follows from the gas area. A locally prismatic channel\nmeets an engine-axis-normal plane in the image of its section swept along the\nflow direction, so in a local radial/circumferential frame that projection is</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/thrust_chamber/CoolingCircuit.html#pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.CoolingCircuit\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.CoolingCircuit\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">CoolingCircuit</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">contour</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">cross_section</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">span</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#list\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">list</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">placement</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">channel_height</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">walls</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">coolant_transport</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">roughness</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">hot_gas_surface_area_multiplier</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">outer_walls</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">enable_fin</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">bool</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">True</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">rib_material</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Simulation-only representation of a cooling circuit.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">walls</span></code> are ordered from hot gas to coolant. Any <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">role=\"liner\"</span></code>\nlayers precede the main layers; at least one main layer is required.\nWall-like objects without a role are treated as main layers.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">enable_fin=True</span></code> enables this circuit\u2019s rib/fin heat-transfer model.\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">rib_material</span></code> optionally supplies its material (with <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">get_k(T)</span></code>).\nWhen omitted, the coolant-facing main-wall material is used. Disabling\nfins removes their thermal enhancement, not their channel geometry.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#open-interleave-boundaries\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Open interleave boundaries<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#open-interleave-boundaries\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p>When rounded channels are present, an internal boundary where circuits enter\nor leave a shared span is an interleave site. The wall is omitted on both\nsides of that boundary. The steady shared span between boundaries retains its\nrounded/mixed wall; the transition itself is left for manual CAD work.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">--hot-wall-transition-fraction</span></code> sets the <strong>total width</strong> of each empty zone as\na fraction of the full contour axial length. This is the same convention the\nformer blend zone used. The default <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">0.02</span></code> makes each gap 2% of the contour\nlength, centered on its interleave boundary: 1% lies on each side. Python\ninserts exact profiles at the cut positions, independent of coolant sampling.\nOverlapping zones merge, and zones reaching a contour end are clipped. A span\nfully consumed by zones produces no hot wall. Squared-only exports need no\ninterleave cuts because their plain contour is continuous.</p>", "a[href=\"#rib-heat-transfer\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Rib heat transfer<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#rib-heat-transfer\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Set <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">enable_fin</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">rib_material</span></code> on each <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">CoolingCircuit</span></code> independently:</p>", "a[href=\"#squared-channels\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Squared channels<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#squared-channels\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Squared sections use planes perpendicular to the engine axis, for both\nstraight and helical channels. Each origin sits on the base-point path, and the\nfirst in-plane axis points radially outward. Consequently the engine axis is at\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(-r_base,</span> <span class=\"pre\">0)</span></code> in local plane coordinates. The channel floor and roof are exact\ncircles about that point.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">build_axis_normal_section_planes(path)</span></code> provides these planes directly.\nThey are also available through <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">CoolingCircuit.section_planes(axis_normal=True)</span></code>\nand <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ResolvedChannel.axis_normal_section_planes</span></code>. The original flow-normal\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">section_planes</span></code> interfaces retain their behavior.</p>", "a[href=\"#hot-wall-export\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Hot-wall export<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#hot-wall-export\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>The advanced and RL10 entry points share the same exporter and version 8 JSON\ncontract. Every export includes the hot wall:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/common/solids/index.html#pyskyfire.common.solids.GRCop42\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.common.solids.GRCop42\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.common.solids.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">GRCop42</span></span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"#the-three-paths\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">The three paths<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#the-three-paths\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>A circuit carries three cylindrical <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(x,</span> <span class=\"pre\">r,</span> <span class=\"pre\">theta)</span></code> paths, and they answer\nthree different questions.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">reference_path</span></code> is the ideal contour carrying the nominal winding. Its radius\nis <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">contour.r(x)</span></code> exactly, and its angular rate comes from the placement\u2019s\nhelix law. Nothing about the cross section or the wall stack enters it, which\nis the point: two circuits asking for the same helix angle wind together and\ncannot drift apart, whatever sections they carry.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/plot_regen/PlotChannelHeight.html#pyskyfire.viz.plot_regen.PlotChannelHeight\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.plot_regen.PlotChannelHeight\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.plot_regen.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">PlotChannelHeight</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">thrust_chamber</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">circuit_index</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/plot_regen/index.html#pyskyfire.viz.plot_regen.IndexLike\" title=\"pyskyfire.viz.plot_regen.IndexLike\"><span class=\"pre\">IndexLike</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">height</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'full'</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/core/PlotBase.html#pyskyfire.viz.core.PlotBase\" title=\"pyskyfire.viz.core.PlotBase\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.core.PlotBase</span></code></a></p><p>Plot full internal coolant height, or optionally rounded base height.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">height=\"full\"</span></code> (default) reports full height even when a rounded\nsection accepts base-height input. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">height=\"base\"</span></code> reports only the\nlegacy base parameter; <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">height=\"both\"</span></code> overlays both with distinct\nlabels and line styles. Squared sections have equal full/base heights.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/cross_section/CrossSectionRounded.html#pyskyfire.regen.cross_section.CrossSectionRounded\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cross_section.CrossSectionRounded\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cross_section.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">CrossSectionRounded</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n_points</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">16</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">height_input</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'full'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">exposure</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">exposure_angles</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">enable_fin</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">False</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ChannelSection</span></code></p><p>Two circular lobes connected by straight tangent sidewalls.</p><p>Both input routes build the same boundary: sector radius/angle/wall\nthickness, or internal floor and roof endpoint widths and height. Equal\nwidths give parallel sides; equal widths with full height equal to width\ngive a circle. A single wall thickness offsets all four surfaces.</p><p>height_input=\u201dfull\u201d measures bottom-to-top passage height; \u201cbase\u201d measures\nseparation of lobe centres. For unequal endpoint widths and full height,\nthe less steep of the two possible tangent constructions is selected.\nInvalid combinations raise rather than distorting the lobes. Angular\ninput retains its exact prescribed sidewall angle.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#main-walls-and-liners\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Main walls and liners<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#main-walls-and-liners\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Wall</span></code> accepts <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">role=\"main\"</span></code> (the default) or <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">role=\"liner\"</span></code>:</p>", "a[href=\"#rounded-and-mixed-spans\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Rounded and mixed spans<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#rounded-and-mixed-spans\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p>A span containing rounded channels uses <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">hotWall.sections</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">hotWall.runs</span></code>.\nEach run names the same channels in the same order at every section, and\nFeatureScript lofts each curve along its run separately. This retains the\nhelical correspondence, including the squared pieces in mixed profiles.\nSquared-only spans elsewhere in the same chamber still use revolves.</p><p>Within each circumferential profile, squared pieces on the same contour join\ndirectly over the ribs. Squared/rounded and rounded/rounded neighbours are\ntrimmed and joined by tangent cubic B\u00e9zier curves. The endpoint handles follow\nthe adjoining tangents and have length one third of their separation.\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">--hot-wall-trim-fraction</span></code> controls how much of each arc\u2019s parameter span is\nremoved from <strong>each blended side</strong>, in <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(0,</span> <span class=\"pre\">0.5)</span></code> (default 0.1). It is not a\nfraction of physical elliptical arc length. Closure and angular folds are\nchecked before export.</p>", "a[href=\"#plain-walls-and-full-contour-coverage\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Plain walls and full-contour coverage<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#plain-walls-and-full-contour-coverage\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p>Where all active channels are squared, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">hotWall.revolves</span></code> supplies the\nmeridional chamber contour for a full revolution about the thrust-chamber\naxis. Straight and helical squared channels use the same surface. Each smooth\nrun of the contour is exported as one spline through the contour\u2019s own knots,\nwhich Onshape fits with <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">skFitSpline</span></code>, so the revolved wall is a single smooth\nface rather than a chain of short segments. Runs are cut wherever the meridian\u2019s\ntangent jumps, keeping the independent slopes on either side of the throat, and\na run left with a single interval falls back to the cubic B\u00e9zier that\nreproduces that interval exactly.</p><p>By default, these surfaces cover the union of the selected circuit spans.\nOverlapping or touching squared spans share a revolve; uncovered gaps remain\nopen. If <strong>all exported circuits are squared</strong>, <strong>Cover entire hot wall</strong>\nappears in Onshape. It defaults off. Enabling it replaces the covered-span\nrevolves with one revolution of the full chamber contour, including uncovered\nends and internal gaps. The option is hidden when any exported channel is\nrounded. A circuit subset is evaluated on the channels included in its JSON.</p>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
